Russia says President Vladimir Putin is  expected to attend the massive military  exercises underway right now in Eastern  Europe Russia and Belarus are staging  the simulated conflict involving troops  tanks and aircrafts NATO says the war  games near the Baltic Sea involve about  a hundred thousand military personnel it  includes firing nuclear capable  ballistic missiles Moscow claims the war  games pose no threat Elizabeth Palmer  will travel over the weekend with the  Russian military for an up-close look at  the drills she joins us now from London  Elizabeth good morning good morning  Russia stages these huge military  exercises every four years but this one  is different and it's more provocative  because the troops will be deployed  outside Russia and neighbouring Belarus  to the west and that means they'll be  along almost a thousand miles of border  with several NATO countries where there  is already a beefed up military presence  including 4,000 US personnel Russia's  exercises will involve as you mentioned  it's Army its Navy and it's Air Force  and electronic warfare troops the  Kremlin insists the exercises are  defensive not cover for an invasion like  we saw in Crimea for example and US  commanders believe that's true relations  between Russia and the West may be  hostile at the moment but there's no  sign Russia wants to pick a fight  however it does want to very publicly  flex its muscles as a warning that if  push came to shove it would be a  formidable opponent Jeff this Palmer  thank you
 

